  "description": "Spanning forest with cost type T; requires >>uf. _mst<T=ll> uses T for edge costs and ret(). Constraints require a mutable T to support += with a const T&, and < to produce a bool-convertible result. T must also support default construction to the additive identity, copying and assignment. add(u,v,cost) returns a stable zero-based edge ID. Public struct edge stores s,e,c; get_edge(id) returns a const reference to the original edge, selected or not. build(components=1,maximum=false) recomputes the minimum forest by default, or maximum when true, stopping at the requested component count when reachable. It returns false if disconnected input prevents the target; ret() and it_edge() then expose the maximum-cardinality forest produced. Equal costs are ordered by insertion ID in both modes. ret() returns the cached total; it_edge(f) calls f(id,u,v,cost) on selected original edges in selection order. result is initialized from T{} and accumulates costs directly using += in T; intermediate totals must fit T, so choose i128 when needed. Rebuild after adding input, and clear(n,base=1) resets inputs and IDs. Vertex n is the maximum external index. Build is O(n+m log m), get_edge/ret O(1), and iteration O(selected edges)."
